---
export const title = 'Usage';
export const order = 100;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';
---

<p>
  <code>wc-datetime-field</code> is a text field for a date and a time. Its picker shows the calendar
  and the time columns side by side, and stays open so both can be set; the value is committed with
  <code>change</code> when the picker closes. Picking a date keeps the time, and picking a time first
  uses today's date.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <div style='width: 100%; max-width: 320px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1rem;'>
    <wc-datetime-field id='datetime-field-demo' label='Meeting' value='2026-11-06T09:30' step='15'></wc-datetime-field>
    <wc-datetime-field label='Deadline' min='2026-11-06T09:00' helper-text='From November 6, 9:00 AM'></wc-datetime-field>
  </div>
  <script is:inline>
    document.querySelector('#datetime-field-demo').addEventListener('change', function (event) {
      myConsole.log('change :: ' + event.detail.value);
    });
  </script>
</DemoComponentCard>

<p>
  Type the date and the time with a comma or a space between them, such as
  <code>11/6/2026, 9:30 am</code>. The value is a local ISO date-time
  (<code>2026-11-06T09:30</code>), and the field is form-associated.
</p>
